Observability: SDD

Purpose:
  Observability technology catalog with monitoring, logging, tracing,
  and alerting options. Root stack/ defines reusable observability knowledge;
  projects/{project_name}/stack/ stores the selected observability stack for the project.

Catalog:
  Prometheus:
    Type: Metrics
    Pros:
      - Open source
      - Pull-based
      - Multi-dimensional data model
      - Alertmanager integration
    Cons:
      - No long-term storage
      - No native distributed tracing
    BestFor:
      - Container metrics
      - Service monitoring
      - Alerting
    AvoidWhen:
      - Long-term metrics storage
    Integration:
      - Node exporter
      - Grafana
      - Alertmanager

  Grafana:
    Type: Visualization
    Pros:
      - Rich dashboards
      - Multi-datasource
      - Alerting
      - Open source
    Cons:
      - Learning curve for complex dashboards
    BestFor:
      - Metrics visualization
      - Operations dashboards
      - SLA monitoring
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple metrics

  Loki:
    Type: Logging
    Pros:
      - LogQL query language
      - Grafana integration
      - Cost-effective
      - Labels for indexing
    Cons:
      - Full-text search limited
      - Newer than ELK
    BestFor:
      - Application logs
      - Kubernetes logs
      - Cost-sensitive logging
    AvoidWhen:
      - Complex log analytics

  Jaeger:
    Type: Distributed Tracing
    Pros:
      - Open source
      - CNCF project
      - OpenTracing compatible
      - Kubernetes native
    Cons:
      - Storage overhead
      - Sampling complexity
    BestFor:
      - Microservice tracing
      - Performance debugging
      - Distributed systems
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple monoliths

  OpenTelemetry:
    Type: Observability Framework
    Pros:
      - Vendor-neutral
      - Signals: metrics, logs, traces
      - Wide language support
      - CNCF project
    Cons:
      - Still maturing
      - Setup complexity
    BestFor:
      - Modern observability
      - Vendor portability
      - Multi-signal correlation
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple single-signal needs

  Sentry:
    Type: Error Tracking
    Pros:
      - Excellent error grouping
      - Release tracking
      - Performance monitoring
      - Multi-language
    Cons:
      - Cost at scale
      - Data retention limits
    BestFor:
      - Application error tracking
      - Performance monitoring
      - Release health
    AvoidWhen:
      - Free tier only

SelectionRules:
  - Metrics: need for metrics collection and alerting
  - Logs: logging volume and retention requirements
  - Traces: distributed tracing needs
  - Budget: observability budget constraints
  - Integration: compatibility with existing stack
  - TeamFit: existing observability expertise

TechnologyScore:
  Metrics: 0-25
  Logs: 0-20
  Traces: 0-15
  Budget: 0-10
  Integration: 0-15
  TeamFit: 0-15

State: +
  
